# Hi-Fi Design Generator (Cursor rule)

This is an **Agent-Requested** rule: `alwaysApply: false` means Cursor pulls it in
only when the task matches the `description` above, so it stays out of unrelated
prompts — the same on-demand behavior as a Claude skill.

When this rule fires, follow the full workflow in the referenced files. Do not
improvise a shortcut — the discipline (tight brief → wide net → refine → tweaks bar)
is the point.

- Follow the workflow in @docs/hifi-design.md end to end.
- Read @docs/design-quality.md before generating the first design — it is the
  anti-slop guardrail layer.
- Embed @docs/tweaks-bar.html in every refinement-stage output (Steps 3–4).

**Non-negotiables:** standalone HTML (all CSS/JS inline, no build step, CDN
fonts/icons only); token-first (`--accent`, `--font-scale`, `--space-scale`,
`--radius` on `:root`); real copy, never lorem ipsum; collect all four brief inputs
before generating.
